          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it safe to look at a laser level beam?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Do not stare into the beam or point it at anyone's eyes. Most construction line lasers are Class 2 or 3R, which are considered safe for normal use because the natural blink reflex protects you from a brief accidental glance. Deliberate staring, or viewing through binoculars or a level, is not safe."
